<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to fall.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields continue to fall.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan treasury bill yields continued to fall at Tuesday's auction, with weighted average of three, six and 12-month bills falling by 1.18 percentage points, 0.78 and 0.50 respectively, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		   bids received   bids accepted   avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     6,252	     2,370	  13.98 (15.16)</p>
<p>    6 months     2,595	     1,243	  15.00 (15.78)</p>
<p>    12 months    2,478	     2,283	  15.30 (15.80)</p>
<p>    Total	 11,325	     5,896</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in million rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). -- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
